{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), evidence is extremely sparse. The most fundamental uncertainty for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether the image modality carries independent predictive signal. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly tests this: if image-only accuracy is substantially higher than 0.485, it confirms the image channel is informative and justifies investing subsequent budget in multimodal fusion configurations; if it is similarly low, it suggests the task is intrinsically difficult or that neither single modality suffices, redirecting effort toward better encoders or multiprofile aggregation. ResNet50 is chosen over ViT-L as the lighter, more standard first probe. This experiment reduces the largest structural uncertainty (modality contribution) before committing budget to the many multimodal combinations, making it the highest-information next step under a limited budget."
}

